How to run the project
After adding and committing these files to GitHub, download or clone the repository to your computer.
1. Install dependencies:
pip install -r requirements.txt

2. Start the local webpage from the project folder:
python -m http.server 8000

3. Open a second terminal in the same folder and execute:
python -m pytest -v

4. Generate an XML report if needed:
python -m pytest -v --junitxml=test-results.xml

NOTE: The test code assumes Google Chrome is installed and Selenium Manager can configure its driver. These are sample project files; run the tests before claiming they passed.
